% Bibliography for QuantArtifact.
%
% PROVENANCE: every entry below was fetched from the arXiv API (or the ACL
% Anthology) rather than written from memory, on 2026-08-26. Titles, author
% lists and venues are verbatim. This matters more than usual here: task `C1`
% turns on differentiating precisely against these papers, and a
% mischaracterised neighbour is the failure mode that gets the paper rejected.
%
% Where a paper is preprint-only with no venue, that is recorded honestly rather
% than dressed up -- `EXECUTOR-TASKS.md` C1 requires being "generous and
% factual, not dismissive" about the weaker neighbours.
%
% ⚠️ TWO RULES ABOUT COMMENTS IN THIS FILE. Both were learned the hard way, and
% both fail SILENTLY -- tectonic reports only "errors were issued by BibTeX, but
% were ignored" and still emits a PDF with citations quietly missing. Always
% check the rendered entry count, never just that the build succeeded.
%
% 1. Commentary goes OUTSIDE an entry, never between its braces. Inside an
%    entry a percent sign is not a comment: BibTeX reads the text as a field
%    name, says "You're missing a field name", and skips the rest of the entry.
%
% 2. NEVER put an at-sign in a comment. BibTeX has no comment character at the
%    top level -- it ignores everything except an at-sign, which always begins a
%    new entry. A line here reading "keep notes above the <at-sign>" was itself
%    parsed as an entry and swallowed the next real one.


